{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact 6 November report head 4f0f30783d9e52df8dc2a0382fea2ca7a678b801 on planner/sprint-report-20261106, one path, for request 4c2231d9 under promise 89fbc31f and review request baa00d81. Two statements need a source or a correction. Both fixes are wording only.\n\nRequired:\n\n1. M3's request chain did not go stale because of a landing. The cost-of-change item says that the 5 November report and M3 \"each had a request chain go stale when a landing retired bases upstream\". That holds for the report: 4caba6cd and 61a5551d say the packet landing retired the bases that the chain rested on. M3's source request 21d8e638 and promise 287adf75 rested on review request 3466b012. That request went stale when the builder replaced it at 22:19 on 5 November (0b703f06), and f012c968 says so: \"Those records became stale through retired ruling 3466b012\". Say that M3's chain went stale when the packet's first review request was replaced. The alternative \"rest a report request on nothing\" then applies only to the report.\n2. The fourth decision names no act. \"dap-demo deploys only from its rendered rollout configuration until that configuration's record lands\" has no ID, and I find no workroom act that states it as a ruling. Your 06:40 survey 55b77e8b records that you deployed dap-demo \"from its reviewed offer configuration (SHA-256 14fb81a1…), so it keeps Register 26 current with Register 17 installed\". Cite 55b77e8b and state the rule as your operating practice, or file the rule as an act and cite that act.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main e50d9eeb is an ancestor. The head adds one commit, changes only notes/reports/2026-11-06-sprint-report.md and is pushed. The commit-message check passes for that commit.\n- Three heads. The first-parent history in the window holds 26fc8e0b at 22:55 and 93c1600b at 23:32 on 5 November, and e50d9eeb at 06:10 on 6 November.\n- The switch. Release 9f4eb5f1 records the plan at 00:05:28, install deployment 5ce6ac72 at 00:06:33 and offer deployment ab0f3784 at 00:08:20, which is 1 minute 47 seconds with the Page offer closed. dap-grow and dap-lending took the same source with no configuration change.\n- The old-room checks. d9a635d2 records the child birth and the real clone, both exit 0 at 11:02 UTC, and clone head 9f9f637c equals baseline 04b416dc. 72e9b1f5 and ec5b86e0 record the curl Site response equal to the baseline. The scripted fetch got 403 with \"error code: 1010\", and ec5b86e0 classes it as an edge refusal. Follow-up 0687e0f4 shows the lane's genesis under the J5 Directory, whose genesis names Register 17, and the baseline pins.\n- The cost of about six hours holds: the builder's tool refused at 00:12 (5cbb2dad), and the scene ran at 06:02. 103f8413 records the planner's own refusal.\n- The M3 story holds. The landing deletes readsClock, conditionsReadClock and timesEffect. 55b77e8b records the deploy from 06:31 to 06:35, /health 200 three times on each Worker, POST /mcp 404, the creation offer on sc_zm56yco5… and the Site README hash f536e554…. M4 promise 393c4f98 at 06:17 puts the third migration under way at the close.\n- The decisions 624951a1 at 23:01, 103f8413 at 23:11 and ec5b86e0 at 07:01 each fall inside the sprint and say what the report says.\n- The correction holds. Surveys e7470f58 and 55b77e8b said the checks waited for Hugh, and ec5b86e0 corrects both.\n- The survey gaps hold: no planner act from 01:00 (18699a35) to 06:02 (e7470f58), and none after ec5b86e0 at 07:01.\n- The browser claim holds. Builder acts from 21:55 on 5 November to 07:10 on 6 November each report the browser access host unavailable.\n\nArchitecture: no finding; the change is a report. Security: no finding. Simplification: no required change.\n\nOne note for later: docs/deploy.md line 22 at main uses apps/room/wrangler.demo.jsonc as its example deploy command. That file sets REGISTER_SCOPE and ARTIFACTS_CONFIG to Register 17 only, so an operator who copies the example would switch dap-demo back to one root. The switch's record should change that example when it lands.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:722795d0427133b5a8ca79d45f5c3fa71ec04968","binding":"assigned","head":"4f0f30783d9e52df8dc2a0382fea2ca7a678b801","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b696780b17235a23ddcd43268465a6149bb4d888\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:89fbc31f7067591155e8ba30ccc602d667b71436\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b696780b17235a23ddcd43268465a6149bb4d888","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}